 "_about": "ENG34 (2026-11-07, owner 19:25: \"classify skills as melee or ranged. Then a lot of effects will be based on whether they are melee or ranged\"). delivery: every skill (and each damage-dealing custom action, as action:<key>) is melee (a swing or contact strike), ranged (a shot, throw or remote hit) or none (no hit of its own: auras, Armor, Regeneration, field and tick damage, riders). swing: skills that make the unit's OWN swing a ranged attack. rides: for an on-hit or on-being-hit effect, which hits carry it (melee = every melee hit: the swing and every melee-class skill hit; ranged = every ranged hit; any = every hit; swing = the unit's own swing only). against: for a defence, which hits it answers or stops. Effect keys that are not skills in the list (venomous, puncture, freeze, sleep, paralyze, blind, tipsy, confuse, shock, stagger, scar) are old or card-only effect keys the engine still reads. notes: why, for the edge cases. The engine reads this file (bramblewood-engine.js SKILL_DELIVERY); the workbook's Skills tab shows it. The basic lane attack is \"attack\": melee. ENG35 (2026-11-07): the delivery lists the fused keys only (canonical/skill-params.json); a part of a skill (almanacGrant, arrowPoison, deliveryRes ...) is delivered as its skill is (the engine's skillDeliveryOf reads the alias).",
